= Wave 0: First Steps

== Your Story

You are *Cadet [Name]*, top of your class at the Terrene Protectorate Academy. Six years of training. Thousands of simulations. Countless hours in the Matter Manipulator certification lab.

None of it prepared you for this.

The assignment came through this morning — a standard graduation posting to a Protectorate outpost in the Epsilon Sector. Routine. Safe. The kind of assignment every new graduate gets.

Your duffel is packed. Your Matter Manipulator is freshly calibrated. Your shuttle leaves in twenty minutes.

You take one last look at the academy grounds — the spires of Earth's last great institution silhouetted against a pale morning sky — and you cannot shake the feeling that nothing will be routine about this.

== Setting the Tone

Wave 0 is about *discovery*. You are learning everything for the first time — how to survive on alien worlds, how to build, how to fight. The universe is vast and indifferent, but it is also beautiful. Every planet is a new mystery. Every ruin holds a story.

Play at your own pace. Read every codex entry. Build that unnecessary balcony on your ship. The story will wait.

#concept[
  *Roleplaying tip:* Keep an in-character journal. Write a few lines after each session about what your cadet discovered, who they met, and how they feel about their first real assignment. It adds surprising depth to the experience.
]

== Wave 0 Mod Loadout

Only two categories of mods are active in this wave:

- *QoL and UI* — Improvements to inventory management, the SAIL interface, and the starmap. No new items. No balance changes. Just a smoother experience.
- *Bugfixes* — Community patches for known issues in Starbound 1.4.4 that were never officially fixed.

#tip[
  If you are tempted to add more mods, resist. Wave 0 is about experiencing Starbound as it was designed. Wave 1 will give you all the content you crave.
]
